---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="When your agent misbehaves, say this."
  description="A phrasebook for non-technical operators building real software with AI agents. Pick what your agent is doing, get the exact words to say back. Distilled from 1,073 working sessions."
  pageType="home"
>
  <div class="container grid-bg">
    <div class="titleblock">
      <div class="cell">
        <div class="kicker">Document</div>
        <div class="val">The Solo Operator's Manual</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <div class="kicker">For</div>
        <div class="val">Non-technical operators</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <div class="kicker">Revision</div>
        <div class="val">2026-05-15</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <div class="kicker">Refreshed</div>
        <div class="val">Monthly</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <div class="kicker">Status</div>
        <div class="val">Living</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="kicker">How to talk to your AI agent when it gets stubborn</p>
    <h1 class="h-display cover">When your agent<br />misbehaves, say this.</h1>
    <p class="subtle">A phrasebook for operators who don't write code.</p>

    <p class="thesis">
      If you don't write code but you ship software with AI agents, the work eventually comes down
      to this: knowing what to say back when the agent stalls, lies, hands the decision back to you,
      or quietly makes something up. This is the phrasebook for those moments.
    </p>

    <button
      type="button"
      class="cmd-trigger"
      onclick="document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('cmd-palette-open'))"
      aria-label="Open command palette"
    >
      <span class="cmd-trigger-leader">&gt;</span>
      <span class="cmd-trigger-text">Search the manual</span>
      <span class="cmd-trigger-kbd"><kbd>&#8984;</kbd><kbd>K</kbd></span>
    </button>

    <section class="modes" aria-labelledby="modes-heading">
      <h2 id="modes-heading" class="sr-only">Three ways to read this manual</h2>
      <a href="/phrasebook" class="mode primary">
        <span class="badge">PRIMARY</span>
        <h3>The Phrasebook</h3>
        <p class="lead">
          Pick the closest thing your agent is doing. Get the exact words to say back, a short
          explanation of why those words work, and the story of where this pattern came from. This
          is the part you'll use every day.
        </p>
        <span class="cta">Browse the phrasebook &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/start-here" class="mode">
        <span class="badge">IF YOU'RE NEW</span>
        <h3>Start Here</h3>
        <p class="lead">
          Five foundational moves before you need the phrasebook. Read these once and the rest will
          make sense.
        </p>
        <span class="cta">Read the basics &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/about" class="mode">
        <span class="badge">ABOUT</span>
        <h3>Where this came from</h3>
        <p class="lead">
          A non-technical operator. Real software, shipped. The hard moves, written down.
        </p>
        <span class="cta">Read the story &rarr;</span>
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="spec" aria-label="Corpus shape">
      <div class="cell">
        <div class="kicker">Sessions distilled</div><div class="val">1,073</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="kicker">Projects covered</div><div class="val">46</div></div>
      <div class="cell">
        <div class="kicker">Behaviors catalogued</div><div class="val">145</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="kicker">Principles named</div><div class="val">80</div></div>
    </section>

    <div class="rev-strip">
      <span>FRONTISPIECE</span>
      <span>NEXT MONTHLY REFRESH: 2026-06-01</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
